    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Six hundred and forty-two people were watching when Emily took off her sleep mask. They continued watching as she opened an energy drink for breakfast. They watched her walk into the bathroom, the only corner of her apartment not on camera. A viewer typed, “Where is Emily?” It was the only quiet moment she would have all day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This was the morning of Day 1,137 of Emily’s life of streaming. For three years, the 28-year-old has broadcast her life nonstop. She has broadcast every birthday and holiday, every sick day and sleepless night, almost all of it alone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This effort has earned Emily a large following on Twitch, one of the world’s most popular live-streaming platforms. It has also earned her a good amount of money: $5.99 per month from thousands of subscribers, plus "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "donations",
            "ref": "v-donation"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and tips."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Creators like Emily are known as marathon streamers. They are a recent invention of the internet age. No one tells streamers when to record or when to stop. Many streamers have discovered the key to success on their own: The more you share, the more successful you can be."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“They’re "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "judged",
            "ref": "v-judge"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " all the time. They don’t get a break from their viewers. They’re under pressure to be real... and not to be boring, even though real life is often boring,” said Sarah Banet-Weiser, a media professor. “Is it any wonder these people "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "burn out"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "?”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sometimes, Emily doesn’t feel like waking up and clocking into the reality show that is her life. She knows staring at screens all night is unhealthy. When she’s too "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "depressed",
            "ref": "v-depressed"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to stream, she lies in bed for hours while her viewers watch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But she worries that taking a break would be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "disastrous",
            "ref": "v-disastrous"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for her career. Some viewers already complain that she showers for too long, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sleeps in",
            "zh": "睡懒觉"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " too late, and isn’t fun enough."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It feels wrong to complain about her life, but Emily has begun to wonder what she "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "owes",
            "ref": "v-owe"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " her viewers. What should she offer them in return for their money and attention? For those experiencing her life through a screen, is their relationship real or just a dream? And is she even living a life at all, or just performing one?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
